You need to remember that the game is turn-based and not a real-time FPS 
requiring twitching and hand-eye coordination.

So you see that purple h approaching, hit semicolon and look at it because 
it's a free action. Check your inventory which is a free action.

If it's a mindflayer, do you have a helmet? Is it greased? No? Is there a 
nearby stairway? Do you have a magical item that can move you out of harm's 
way?

A bunch of rothes are heading towards you find a hallway and make your 
stand one at a time. Also make sure that you're attacking a Mordor orc 
instead of a floating eye by taking a moment to give a second glance at 
that dark blue round letter.

I rarely use Elbereth and when I do it's only to corral a bunch of monsters 
near an altar.

Once a level is empty of monsters head to the next level. I usually spend a 
bit more than 300 turns on DL1 and start getting weak from hunger around 
DL4 which is around the 880 turn mark.


